<title>SINGAPORE: Pertama full year slips S$3.9 mln into red.</title>
<headline>Pertama full year slips S$3.9 mln into red.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 3.95  vs   0.54 (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.25  vs   1.25</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	  (loss)  4.40  vs   0.60 (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover			     196.32  vs 222.08</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.48  vs   0.57</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.81  vs   2.09</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     1.74  vs   1.81</p>
<p>    Profits from associates  (loss)  0.22  vs   0.04</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   2.82  vs   1.26 (gain)</p>
<p>    Tax					0.91  vs   0.76</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: To be advised</p>
<p>Last day books open: To be advised</p>
<p>Note - Consumer electronics and communications equipment distributor Pertama Holdings Ltd said performance was hit by difficult retail and wholesale trading conditions. It expects conditions to continue to be difficult throughout the region.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
